    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.1. Number of policy documents developed with UNDP assistance that strengthen HRBA approaches to design and delivery of citizen-oriented digital services (including complex services around life situations)

1.2. The level of government employee (including officers at Centres for Administrative Service Provision) awareness of HRBA / inclusivity approaches to the delivery of digital services

1.3. Number of government officials who have undergone UNDPdesigned capacitybuilding courses, events and trainings on design and implementation of citizen-oriented services in line with HRBA and gender mainstreaming principles

2.1. Number of software packages that, when deployed by MDT enable vulnerable citizen-groups to enjoy digital service provision in a given life situation

2.2. Share of users who receive the service package in question through digital means as opposed to the traditional paper-based way

3.1. Share of users who are satisfied by the way that the offered digitalised service package is functioning

3.2. Share of citizens who, having benefitted from the UNDP-designed awareness-raising materials, report an increase in their digital skills due to this support</narrative>
    </description>
